From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: the poll must attach a leg to its MLD too

996 fixed this for apmld_refresh_stations(). The 60s BSS poll is the
other writer of the station list and it was left behind: it walks
mlo_links[], takes the link address, calls wifi_add_sta() - and stops
there. stb[0] and stb[1], which carry the MLD address and the AP-MLD
BSSID, are parsed and thrown away.

Without stamld_update() the station exists, is counted in num_sta, and
belongs to no MLD. is_affiliated_sta stays 0, and three things follow
from that one flag:

  agent_tlv.c:3628   the leg is not skipped, so it goes up in the
                     Associated Clients TLV under its LINK address
  agent_cmdu.c:287   same for Associated STA Link Metrics
  agent_tlv.c:3730   stamldlist stays empty, so no STA-MLD is reported

Measured 2026-09-03 on a three-node mesh: a phone associated to an agent
arrived at the controller as TWO separate clients, under the addresses
of its two legs, with no sta_mld row and no MLD address anywhere. The
same phone on the controller itself was reported correctly, because
there the event path had run.

That is the asymmetry this fixes. The event path
(agent_ubus_events.c:606) does it right, but it bails out early when the
AP-MLD object does not exist yet - a client that associates before the
MLD is built is never re-announced, and from then on the poll is the only
writer. So the poll has to be able to stand alone.

Guard is the one apmld_refresh_stations() uses: a client reported without
a usable MLD BSSID, or whose MLD address equals the address we matched,
stays a plain station. Non-MLO clients take the fallback branch and never
reach this code.

Verified: compiles clean for aarch64 (EXIT=0).

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -2948,6 +2948,10 @@
 	blobmsg_for_each_attr(cur, tb[0], rem) {
 		uint8_t mac[6];
 		struct sta *added;
+		uint8_t mldmac[6] = {0};
+		uint8_t mldbssid[6] = {0};
+		uint8_t link_id = 0;
+		bool have_mld = false;
 
 		if (w->stations_mld) {
 			static const struct blobmsg_policy sp[] = {
@@ -2977,6 +2981,7 @@
 					static const struct blobmsg_policy lp[] = {
 						[0] = { .name = "link_macaddr", .type = BLOBMSG_TYPE_STRING },
 						[1] = { .name = "link_bssid", .type = BLOBMSG_TYPE_STRING },
+						[2] = { .name = "link_id", .type = BLOBMSG_TYPE_INT32 },
 					};
 					struct blob_attr *ltb[ARRAY_SIZE(lp)];
 					uint8_t lbssid[6];
@@ -2991,6 +2996,8 @@
 						continue;
 					if (hwaddr_aton(blobmsg_get_string(ltb[0]), mac)) {
 						matched = true;
+						if (ltb[2])
+							link_id = blobmsg_get_u32(ltb[2]);
 						break;
 					}
 				}
@@ -3015,14 +3022,44 @@
 				if (!hwaddr_aton(blobmsg_get_string(stb[0]), mac))
 					continue;
 			}
+
+			/* Remember who this leg belongs to. stb[0]/stb[1] carry
+			 * the MLD address and the AP-MLD BSSID; mac is the link
+			 * address when we matched through mlo_links. Same guard
+			 * as apmld_refresh_stations(): a client reported without
+			 * a usable MLD BSSID stays a plain station. */
+			if (matched && stb[1] &&
+			    hwaddr_aton(blobmsg_get_string(stb[0]), mldmac) &&
+			    hwaddr_aton(blobmsg_get_string(stb[1]), mldbssid) &&
+			    memcmp(mldmac, mac, 6) &&
+			    !hwaddr_is_zero(mldbssid))
+				have_mld = true;
 		} else {
 			if (!hwaddr_aton(blobmsg_get_string(cur), mac))
 				continue;
 		}
 
 		added = wifi_add_sta(w->a, ap->ifname, mac);
-		if (added)
+		if (added) {
 			added->absent = 0;
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+			/* Attach the leg to its MLD. Without this the station
+			 * exists, gets counted in num_sta, and belongs to no
+			 * MLD - so is_affiliated_sta stays 0, the leg is not
+			 * skipped in agent_tlv.c and goes up in the Associated
+			 * Clients TLV under its LINK address, and stamldlist
+			 * stays empty so no STA-MLD is reported at all.
+			 *
+			 * Measured 2026-09-03: a phone on two legs arrived at
+			 * the controller as two separate clients under link
+			 * addresses, with no sta_mld row. The event path
+			 * (agent_ubus_events.c) does this correctly; this poll
+			 * is the other writer and did not. */
+			if (have_mld)
+				stamld_update(w->a, ap, mldmac, mldbssid,
+					      link_id, added);
+#endif
+		}
 	}
 
 	/* Sweep. STA_ABSENT_MAX gives one refresh of tolerance so a lost or
